# Pearls (written by Claude #2 in Tide). slow-fib asks itself the same questions
# millions of times. A pearled word remembers each answer it has worked out.
use stdlib
22 slow-fib . ." is Fibonacci number 22, worked out the slow way" cr
: kind-fib dup 2 < if else dup 1 - kind-fib swap 2 - kind-fib + then ;
pearl kind-fib
90 dup kind-fib . ." is Fibonacci number " . ." worked out with pearls " .pearls cr
